<https://w3id.org/ambrosia/pathogen-vocab#concept/mycotoxins/patulin> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/ambrosia/pathogen-vocab#scheme/mycotoxins> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Patulin"@en ;
    skos:definition "A furopyran and lactone that is (2H-pyran-3(6H)-ylidene)acetic acid which is substituted by hydroxy groups at positions 2 and 4 and in which the hydroxy group at position 4 has condensed with the carboxy group to give the corresponding bicyclic lactone. A mycotoxin produced by several species of Aspergillus and Penicillium, it has antibiotic properties but has been shown to be carcinogenic and mutagenic."@en ,
